      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, I think the code is correct. AsUid is the UID the request is filed as, while mUid is the true UID of the requestor – this is what the description explains.\n- For an app requesting for itself, mAsUid \u003d\u003d mUid \u003d\u003d the UID of the app.\n- For the system requesting for itself, mAsUid \u003d\u003d mUid \u003d\u003d SYSTEM_UID.\n- For the system requesting for an app, mUid \u003d\u003d SYSTEM_UID and mAsUid \u003d the UID of the app.\n\nAdded comments. Does this clarify ?",
